  "id": "negative-reinforcement",
  "term": "negative reinforcement",
  "definition": "In this packet, negative reinforcement refers to a behavior being maintained because it reduces or dampens an unpleasant internal state, such as intense distress or hyper-arousal. Here, self-injury is described as serving this relief-based function.",
